---
description: Keep test-only helpers in tests/, not in production src/
alwaysApply: true
---

# Test-only helpers

- Do **not** put test-only helpers in `Controller/src/` (or other production trees).
- Put them in the relevant `tests/` file, or `tests/helpers/` if shared across multiple test modules.
- If a function is used by both production and tests, keep it in `src/` with a normal docstring — do not label it “test only”.
- When adding a seam “just for unit tests,” prefer defining it next to the tests unless production code must call it.
